Overview

Rackner is seeking an Associate Data Engineer to provide technical support across data engineering, ETL, platform, and integration workstreams. The Associate Data Engineer will
work on varying tasks such as data extraction, pipeline testing, environment setup, database support, documentation formatting, and technical support activities while also&nbsp;
supporting data population activities including source system data profiling, data cleansing, Ed-Fi ODS loading, and quality validation.

&nbsp;

Responsibilities

• Assists with year-end rollover tasks, data validation, and system configuration under&nbsp;
supervision

• Supports Oracle and SQL Server database management during on premises-to-cloud migration activities

• Assists with SharePoint site development and collaboration platform configuration

• Supports knowledge transfer by producing technical documentation under the&nbsp;
direction of senior staff

Qualifications

• Foundational knowledge of SQL, Python, or Power BI

• Strong organizational and documentation skills

• Cloud platform exposure through coursework, certifications, or prior work

